\ vmain.fam — nodev, the node's verifier (docs/NODE.md, step 10): a
\ process of its own, so the node goes on serving while a block's heavy
\ checks run, on another hart when there is one.  After arith, poseidon2,
\ difficulty, pow and chainver (it shares nothing with the node: its own
\ copy of every buffer).  The node starts it with a pipe on its 0 (jobs)
\ and another on its 1 (verdicts).  A job is a word, its kind, then:
\   0  the proof of work's parameters: items, parents, accesses (3 words)
\   1  a header's full proof of work: the header (204 bytes) and its
\      target (8 words, as headers.fam's htarget leaves it): fullpow
\   2  a chain proof: its 16 public values (words), its length n (a word)
\   	and its n bytes: cvverify
\ each answered (but 0) by a word: the verdict, -1 or 0.  The pipe closed
\ (the node gone), it ends.

: vbuf variable ;  : vcap variable ;  : vwd variable ;  : vh variable ;  : vtg variable ;  : vpub variable ;

\ vfile ( path -- addr n )  a whole data file of at most 1.25 MiB, in memory.
: vfile
dup 0 lit open  dup 0< if drop "nodev: no " puts puts 0A lit putc 1 lit exit then  nip
140000 lit alloc
0 lit begin
	2 lit pick  2 lit pick 2 lit pick +  140000 lit 3 lit pick -  read
	dup 0 lit > while +
repeat drop
rot close drop ;

\ vread ( a n -- )  n bytes from the jobs' pipe; it closed, the end.
: vread
begin dup while
	0 lit 2 lit pick 2 lit pick read  dup 0 lit > 0= if 0 lit exit then
	rot over + -rot -
repeat 2drop ;
: vword  vwd @ 4 lit vread  vwd @ @ ;             \ ( -- x )
: vsay  vwd @ !  1 lit vwd @ 4 lit write drop ;  \ ( x -- )  a verdict

"/lib/akjv.txt.gz" vfile powinit
"/lib/chainver" vfile drop cvinit
10 lit alloc vwd !  CC lit alloc vh !  20 lit alloc vtg !  40 lit alloc vpub !
10000 lit dup vcap ! malloc vbuf !
begin
	vword
	dup 0= if drop  vword pwitems !  vword pwpar !  vword pwacc ! else
	dup 1 lit = if drop  vh @ CC lit vread  vtg @ 20 lit vread  vh @ vtg @ fullpow vsay else
	2 lit = if
		vpub @ 40 lit vread  vword
		dup vcap @ u> if vbuf @ free  dup malloc vbuf !  dup vcap ! then
		vbuf @ over vread
		vpub @ vbuf @ rot cvverify vsay
	else 0 lit exit then then then
0 lit until
